Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:33:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(tests):=20isolate=20real=20~/.lansyncopt=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20Windows=20live-server=20poisoning?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

test-config.js relied on overriding $HOME, but os.homedir() uses
USERPROFILE on Windows: isolation silently failed there while macOS
stayed green (tests looked passing everywhere, yet on any machine
running a live server the suite rewrote the real server.json with a
test token — the daemon re-reads config per request, so the live
server switched tokens instantly and every client call 401'd).

Root fix: module-level LANSNC_CONFIG_DIR=mkdtempSync() in
test-client.js and test-config.js, matching the test-server.js
pattern; the getConfigDir default-path assertion now suspends the
override locally.

Also documented in devlog: the follow-on server stop avalanche
(kills stale pid, deletes config, reports success) is tracked as
server-side hardening work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
